From 34028d0d5b38a454bb0fec9151bf7ddce1df2ae3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: denjiaki <106935517+denjiaki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 12:15:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add plugin action slots, action state, and fix
 packaged-Windows plugin loading

Three related changes to Paseo's plugin system.

1. Composer and message action slots

   Adds `addComposerAction` / `addMessageAction` so a plugin can contribute
   buttons to the composer toolbar and to individual messages, rendered as
   native React components with the app's own styling and accessibility.

2. Optional on/off state for composer actions

   `PluginComposerActionContribution` gains an optional `state` RPC contract
   resolving to `{ active: boolean }`. The host reads it on mount and after
   every successful press, tints the button accordingly, and switches the
   control to `role="switch"` with `checked` so screen readers announce on/off.
   Actions without the contract stay neutral, so this is backward compatible.

3. Packaged Windows builds could not load plugins at all

   The daemon compiles plugins with esbuild, which spawns a native binary.
   electron-builder unpacks that binary to `app.asar.unpacked`, but esbuild
   resolves it relative to its own module path inside `app.asar`, and a binary
   cannot be executed from an asar archive. Every plugin failed to load with
   `spawn ...\esbuild.exe ENOENT`, surfacing as a plugin stuck in `failed`
   rather than as an obvious packaging error.

   `resolvePackagedEsbuildBinaryPath` locates the unpacked binary and the
   daemon env sets `ESBUILD_BINARY_PATH`, esbuild's supported override. An
   explicit value from the environment still wins.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
